{
  "id": "20",
  "pages": 6,
  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        528.4614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        607.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 19 September 1991 two German hikers on a trek in the Ötztal Alps found a corpse by a glacier. It lay on a ridge at about 3,210 metres, on the border between Austria and Italy. The assumption was that a modern-day climber had died on an alpine slope, since glaciers sometimes yield frozen remains."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        440.7614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        519.9614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Taking it for a recent death, rescuers used a jackhammer that ripped flesh from his left hip. His possessions told another story: leather and grass clothing, a copper axe, a bow and arrows, all prehistoric artefacts. Known as Ötzi, the natural mummy was a man who lived about 5,300 years ago, between 3350 and 3105 BC."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        353.0614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        432.2614173228347
      ],
      "text": "In 2001, X-rays revealed a flint arrowhead lodged in his left shoulder, unseen by examiners a decade earlier. A scanner showed that the puncture had ruptured an artery, a mortal injury causing heavy bleeding, and left a large clot. Researchers believe he died within minutes. He was about 46."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        245.5614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        344.5614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Another person, it is thought, killed him. From the wound's depth researchers inferred that an archer shot him from the rear, at about 30 metres. The shooter probably caught him unawares. A 2018 study found he had dined on dried ibex meat and fat, red deer, and einkorn wheat, a hearty, nourishing meal reportedly consumed within two hours of his death."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        157.8614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        237.0614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Curators in Bolzano now keep Ötzi, whose 61 tattoos on joints and spine were perhaps an early form of acupuncture. The archer's identity is an enigma, and any motive is conjecture. Ötzi has a name, a last meal, and a cause of death, while his anonymous killer has none."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        547.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        607.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1991年9月19日，两名德国徒步者在奥茨塔尔阿尔卑斯山远足时，于冰川旁发现一具遗体。它位于奥地利与意大利交界处、海拔约3210米的山脊上。人们最初以为，一名现代登山者死在高山坡地上，毕竟冰川有时会吐露冰冻的遗骸。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        459.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        539.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "救援人员以为这是近期的死亡事件，使用风钻凿冰，结果撕损了死者左侧髋部的皮肉。但他的随身物品讲述了另一种故事：皮革和草编衣物、铜斧、弓箭，全是史前器物。这具被称为奥茨的天然木乃伊是一名男子，生活于约5300年前，即公元前3350至前3105年之间。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        390.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        450.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2001年，X光检查发现一枚燧石箭头嵌在他的左肩里，十年前的检查者并未发现它。扫描显示，穿刺伤撕裂了一条动脉，造成大量出血的致命损伤，并留下一个大血块。研究者认为，他在几分钟内便死亡，当时约46岁。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        302.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "人们认为，他是遭人杀害的。研究者根据伤口深度推断，弓箭手从他背后约30米处射箭，很可能是在他毫无防备时出手。2018年的研究发现，他最后吃过干野山羊肉和脂肪、马鹿肉与单粒小麦。这是一顿丰盛而营养丰富的饭，据报道在死前两小时内吃下。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        213.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        293.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "如今，博尔扎诺的馆藏保管人员保存着奥茨的遗体。他关节和脊柱上的61处文身，也许是一种早期针灸形式。弓箭手的身份仍是谜团，任何作案动机都只是猜测。奥茨有名字、最后一餐和死因；对于那名身份不明的凶手，我们却连这些信息都不知道。"
    }
  ],
